  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Lee Jae-yong (Korean: 이재용; born June 23, 1968) is a South Korean business executive who has served as the executive chairman of Samsung, one of South Korea's most valuable companies. Since joining Samsung in 1991, Lee has since held various positions in the company. According to Forbes, he has been South Korea's wealthiest person with a net worth of over US$20 billion as of November 2026.\nBorn in Washington, D.C. to the family that controls the Samsung conglomerate, Lee graduated from Keio University with a master's degree in business administration. In 2017, Lee was convicted of bribery, embezzlement, and concealment of criminal proceeds. He served a prison sentence until being pardoned by President Yoon Suk Yeol in August 2022 and later in October, he rejoined Samsung to serve as the chairman. He has also been named to Forbes list of the world's top 50 billionaires.",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
